<AddOnInstructionDefinitions Use="Context">
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Use="Target" Name="L_ChangeDet" Revision="3.1" RevisionExtension="01 Release" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="true" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2010-09-27T15:11:59.545Z" CreatedBy="Not Available" EditedDate="2014-09-03T14:26:32.932Z"
 EditedBy="PROCESS\Library" SoftwareRevision="v18.02" SourceKey="eladdrawdedeer" SourceProtectionType="Full Protection">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Logix Change Detector]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details. Unmodified, up-rev only for V3.1-01 public release.]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.

This Instruction monitors a Logix controller for changes.  It can monitor the
controller executing it (although in this case, it cannot report "Program Mode"
or "Keyswitch in Program") or another controller, depending on the Path used
by its CIP Generic Messages, for changes.  The controller executing this
instruction must be firmware Major revision 18 or later.  The controller being
monitored must be firmware Major revision 16 or later.

NOTE:  IT IS UP TO THE USER TO SET THE PATH OF THE Ref_CLMsgCtrl
MSG CONTROL TAG TO POINT TO THE CONTROLLER OF INTEREST!!!

(This MSG Path is automatically copied to the other two MSG control
tags:  Ref_CSMsgCtrl and Ref_DTMsgCtrl.  The required MSG control,
send data, and receive data tags are created for you when this rung
is imported.)

The instruction provides detection of:

* New entries being made in the Change Log.
    (Changes that cause a write to the Change Log object include:
     Set Attribute / SSV, 
     Set Attribute List, or
     Set Attribute All on an object;
     apply Attributes on an object;
     create, delete or reset a controller object / instance;
     modify, insert or delete logic in RUN or PROG Mode;
     accept, assemble or cancel Edits;
     enable, disable or remove Forces;
     reconfigure a Module; and
     change Output List.)
* Downloading of a different application
* Partial Import into an application
* Downloading of an application without logic changes
     (but saved configuration data may have changed)
* Downloading of an application containing offline edits
* Restore of application from Flash (CF or SD card)

This instruction also reports the following:

* a Controller / Application "CHECK" value for change detection;
* the (local) Date and Time on the controller clock (YYYY-MM-DD hh:mm:ss.uuuuuu)
* the Day of the Week based on the controller Date
* the controller Keyswitch position and Mode
* indication of Major and Minor Faults

The interval at which this instruction checks for changes and
updates its status is configurable, for 1 to 60 seconds.
]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
