<LocalTag Name="Wrk_G" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Year offset used in calculating the Day of the Week]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Type" DataType="STRING_16" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Must contain AOI name, used for HMI and Information S/W]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>0B 00 00 00 4C 5F 43 68 61 6E 67 65 44 65 74 00 
00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="11">
<![CDATA['L_ChangeDet']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_MsgErr" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1 = Message Poll errored, did not complete]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Done" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1 = Message Poll completed successfully]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_RestoreFromFlash" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[CHANGE DETECTED: The application was restored from the Flash card (CF/SD)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_EditsDownload" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[CHANGE DETECTED: An application with offline edits was downloaded]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_NoChangeDownload" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[CHANGE DETECTED: The same application was downloaded (config data may have changed)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_ChangeDownload" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[CHANGE DETECTED: A changed application was downloaded]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_OnlineChange" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[CHANGE DETECTED: An online change or partial import]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Tag" DataType="STRING_20" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Tagname for display on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>0B 00 00 00 4C 5F 43 68 61 6E 67 65 44 65 74 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="11">
<![CDATA['L_ChangeDet']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Label" DataType="STRING_20" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Label for graphic symbol displayed on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>0F 00 00 00 43 68 61 6E 67 65 20 44 65 74 65 63 
74 6F 72 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="15">
<![CDATA['Change Detector']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Desc" DataType="STRING_40" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Description for display on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>20 00 00 00 4C 6F 67 69 78 20 43 6F 6E 74 72 6F 
6C 6C 65 72 20 43 68 61 6E 67 65 20 44 65 74 65 
63 74 6F 72 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="32">
<![CDATA['Logix Controller Change Detector']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Lib" DataType="STRING_12" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Display Library for Faceplate call-up]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>06 00 00 00 52 41 2D 42 41 53 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="6">
<![CDATA['RA-BAS']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Step" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Current step # in polling sequence]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Detect changes in a controller (this controller or another, depending on MSG paths)]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
L_ChangeDet:  LOGIX -- CONTROLLER CHANGE DETECTOR
============================================================
Revision 3.1-01 Release  2014-09-03:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib.
V3.0-01  2013-08-06:  Modified sequence to avoid errors when run in a
continuous task.
V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Unmodified for Library of Process Objects V3.1, up-rev only.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Unmodified, up-rev only for V3.1-01 public release.
============================================================
This Instruction monitors a Logix controller for changes.  It can monitor the
controller executing it (although in this case, it cannot report "Program Mode"
or "Keyswitch in Program") or another controller, depending on the Path used
by its CIP Generic Messages, for changes.  The controller executing this
instruction must be firmware Major revision 18 or later.  The controller being
monitored must be firmware Major revision 16 or later.

NOTE:  IT IS UP TO THE USER TO SET THE PATH OF THE Ref_CLMsgCtrl
MSG CONTROL TAG TO POINT TO THE CONTROLLER OF INTEREST!!!

(This MSG Path is automatically copied to the other two MSG control
tags:  Ref_CSMsgCtrl and Ref_DTMsgCtrl.  The required MSG control,
send data, and receive data tags are created for you when this rung
is imported.)

The instruction provides detection of:

* New entries being made in the Change Log.
    (Changes that cause a write to the Change Log object include:
     Set Attribute / SSV, 
     Set Attribute List, or
     Set Attribute All on an object;
     apply Attributes on an object;
     create, delete or reset a controller object / instance;
     modify, insert or delete logic in RUN or PROG Mode;
     accept, assemble or cancel Edits;
     enable, disable or remove Forces;
     reconfigure a Module; and
     change Output List.)
* Downloading of a different application
* Partial Import into an application
* Downloading of an application without logic changes
     (but saved configuration data may have changed)
* Downloading of an application containing offline edits
* Restore of application from Flash (CF or SD card)

This instruction also reports the following:

* a Controller / Application "CHECK" value for change detection;
* the (local) Date and Time on the controller clock (YYYY-MM-DD hh:mm:ss.uuuuuu)
* the Day of the Week based on the controller Date
* the controller Keyswitch position and Mode
* indication of Major and Minor Faults

The interval at which this instruction checks for changes and
updates its status is configurable, for 1 to 60 seconds.
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
HANDLE CONFIGURATION
============================================================
These rungs handle checking of Configuration data for this instruction.

Check the Update Time.  It must be between 1 and 60 seconds.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)[LES(Cfg_UpdateT,1) MOV(1,Cfg_UpdateT) ,GRT(Cfg_UpdateT,60) MOV(60,Cfg_UpdateT) ,MUL(Cfg_UpdateT,1000,Wrk_UpdateT.PRE) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CHANGE DETECTOR DATA UPDATE TIMER
============================================================
This rung is a self repeating timer for triggering
data collection at the Update Time interval.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_UpdateT.DN)TON(Wrk_UpdateT,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ACK ALL COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Ack All command clears all the change detected latch bits.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cmd_AckAll)XIC(Wrk_UpdateT.DN)OTU(Cmd_AckAll)OTU(Wrk_ChangeDownload)OTU(Wrk_NoChangeDownload)OTU(Wrk_EditsDownload)OTU(Wrk_OnlineChange)OTU(Wrk_RestoreFromFlash);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MESSAGES TO CIP OBJECTS IN CONTROLLER
============================================================
Much of the information we need can only be obtianed via CIP GENERIC Messages.

Each update, we set a latch that is held ON undil ALL the messages
to the controller to get performance data have finished or errored.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_UpdateT.DN)OTL(Wrk_Poll)OTU(Wrk_Done)OTU(Wrk_MsgErr)CLR(Wrk_Step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung hard-codes the data in the GetAttributeList MSGs.
For the ChangeLog object, get 6 attributes : #1, 2, 3, 4, 8, and 10.
For the Wallclocktime object, get 1 attribute:  #5.
For the Controller Status object, get 1 attribute:  #5
(To work all the way back to Rev. 12, must use GetAttrList for
these last two, cannot use GetAttrSingle....)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Poll)EQU(Wrk_Step,0)[MOV(6,Ref_CLMsgSrc[0]) MOV(1,Ref_CLMsgSrc[1]) MOV(2,Ref_CLMsgSrc[2]) MOV(3,Ref_CLMsgSrc[3]) ,MOV(4,Ref_CLMsgSrc[4]) MOV(8,Ref_CLMsgSrc[5]) MOV(10,Ref_CLMsgSrc[6]) MOV(0,Ref_CLMsgSrc[7]) ,MOV(14,Ref_CLMsgCtrl.REQ_LEN) MOV(16#00AC,Ref_CLMsgCtrl.Class) MOV(0,Ref_CLMsgCtrl.Attribute) MOV(1,Ref_CLMsgCtrl.Instance) ,MOV(1,Wrk_Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Poll)EQU(Wrk_Step,1)MSG(Ref_CLMsgCtrl);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When the Controller Change Log MSG is done, get the various
indices and UIDs and store them away.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Ref_CLMsgCtrl.EN)[XIC(Ref_CLMsgCtrl.ER) OTL(Wrk_MsgErr) ,XIC(Ref_CLMsgCtrl.DN) [MOV(Wrk_CurrIndex,Wrk_PrevIndex) COP(Ref_CLMsgDest[6],Wrk_CurrIndex,1) ,MOV(Wrk_CurrGen,Wrk_PrevGen) COP(Ref_CLMsgDest[12],Wrk_CurrGen,1) ,MOV(Wrk_CurrSWUID,Wrk_PrevSWUID) COP(Ref_CLMsgDest[18],Wrk_CurrSWUID,1) ,MOV(Wrk_CurrCopyUID,Wrk_PrevCopyUID) COP(Ref_CLMsgDest[26],Wrk_CurrCopyUID,1) ,MOV(Wrk_CurrImgUID,Wrk_PrevImgUID) COP(Ref_CLMsgDest[34],Wrk_CurrImgUID,1) ,MOV(Wrk_CurrTLUID,Wrk_PrevTLUID) COP(Ref_CLMsgDest[42],Wrk_CurrTLUID,1) ] ]MOV(2,Wrk_Step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When each MSG is accepted into the queue and active (.ST), or if we missed ST and
the MSG is done (.DN) or errored (.ER), we can clear the GetAttributeList data to hide it.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Ref_CLMsgCtrl.ST) ,XIC(Ref_CLMsgCtrl.DN) ,XIC(Ref_CLMsgCtrl.ER) ][FLL(0,Ref_CLMsgSrc[0],8) CLR(Ref_CLMsgCtrl.REQ_LEN) ,CLR(Ref_CLMsgCtrl.Class) CLR(Ref_CLMsgCtrl.Attribute) CLR(Ref_CLMsgCtrl.Instance) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Poll)EQU(Wrk_Step,2)[MOV(1,Ref_DTMsgSrc[0]) MOV(5,Ref_DTMsgSrc[1]) MOV(0,Ref_DTMsgSrc[2]) COP(Ref_CLMsgCtrl.Path,Ref_DTMsgCtrl.Path,1) ,MOV(4,Ref_DTMsgCtrl.REQ_LEN) MOV(16#008B,Ref_DTMsgCtrl.Class) MOV(0,Ref_DTMsgCtrl.Attribute) MOV(1,Ref_DTMsgCtrl.Instance) ,MOV(3,Wrk_Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Poll)EQU(Wrk_Step,3)MSG(Ref_DTMsgCtrl);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
REPORT THE DATE AND TIME AND
CALCULATE THE DAY OF THE WEEK
============================================================
When the Date and Time MSG completes,
copy the date and time data (seven DINTs)
and calculate the day of the week.

This version of the day of the week is based on:
http://alcor.concordia.ca/~gpkatch/gdate-algorithm.html

(NOTE:  ALL divisions are INTEGER -- truncated -- divisions!)
F = ( month + 9 ) MOD 12
G = year - ( F / 10 )
Gregorian DayNumber [ D ] = ( 365 * G ) + ( G / 4 ) - ( G / 100 ) + ( G / 400 ) + ( ( ( F * 306 ) + 5 ) / 10 ) + day - 1
DayOfWeek = ( DayNumber + 3 ) MOD 7
(The "-1" and "+3" are combined in the final CPT.)
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Ref_DTMsgCtrl.EN)[XIC(Ref_DTMsgCtrl.ER) OTL(Wrk_MsgErr) ,XIC(Ref_DTMsgCtrl.DN) [MOV(Ref_DTMsgDest[3],Val_Year) MOV(Ref_DTMsgDest[5],Val_Month) MOV(Ref_DTMsgDest[7],Val_Day) ,MOV(Ref_DTMsgDest[9],Val_Hour) MOV(Ref_DTMsgDest[11],Val_Minute) MOV(Ref_DTMsgDest[13],Val_Second) ,BTD(Ref_DTMsgDest[15],0,Val_Microsecond,0,16) BTD(Ref_DTMsgDest[16],0,Val_Microsecond,16,16) ,CPT(Wrk_F,(Val_Month+9)MOD 12) CPT(Wrk_G,Val_Year-(Wrk_F/10)) ,CPT(Val_DayOfWeek,(365*Wrk_G+(Wrk_G/4)-(Wrk_G/100)+(Wrk_G/400)+((Wrk_F*306+5)/10)+Val_Day+2)MOD 7) ] ]MOV(4,Wrk_Step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Ref_DTMsgCtrl.ST) ,XIC(Ref_DTMsgCtrl.DN) ,XIC(Ref_DTMsgCtrl.ER) ][FLL(0,Ref_DTMsgSrc[0],4) CLR(Ref_DTMsgCtrl.REQ_LEN) ,CLR(Ref_DTMsgCtrl.Class) CLR(Ref_DTMsgCtrl.Attribute) CLR(Ref_DTMsgCtrl.Instance) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Poll)EQU(Wrk_Step,4)[MOV(1,Ref_CSMsgSrc[0]) MOV(5,Ref_CSMsgSrc[1]) MOV(0,Ref_CSMsgSrc[2]) COP(Ref_CLMsgCtrl.Path,Ref_CSMsgCtrl.Path,1) ,MOV(4,Ref_CSMsgCtrl.REQ_LEN) MOV(16#0001,Ref_CSMsgCtrl.Class) MOV(0,Ref_CSMsgCtrl.Attribute) MOV(1,Ref_CSMsgCtrl.Instance) ,MOV(5,Wrk_Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Msg to retrieve 6 change log parameters
Change_ Index
Generation_Count
Software_UID
Copy_UID
Image_UID
TimeLine_UID

MSG to get the Controller Date and Time (WALLCLOCKTIME)

MSG to get the Controller Status (Mode, Faults, Keyswitch)

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Poll)EQU(Wrk_Step,5)MSG(Ref_CSMsgCtrl);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
REPORT MSG STATUS WHEN POLL IS COMPLETE
============================================================
If the last MSG errors out, set the Msg Err Status.
Since this is the last MSG, if it's Done or Errored, we're done with polling.
If none of the MSGs errored, flag the poll as successfully DONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Ref_CSMsgCtrl.EN)[XIC(Ref_CSMsgCtrl.ER) OTL(Wrk_MsgErr) ,XIC(Ref_CSMsgCtrl.DN) ][OTU(Wrk_Poll) ,XIO(Wrk_MsgErr) OTL(Wrk_Done) ,MOV(6,Wrk_Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Ref_CSMsgCtrl.ST) ,XIC(Ref_CSMsgCtrl.DN) ,XIC(Ref_CSMsgCtrl.ER) ][FLL(0,Ref_CSMsgSrc[0],4) CLR(Ref_CSMsgCtrl.REQ_LEN) ,CLR(Ref_CSMsgCtrl.Class) CLR(Ref_CSMsgCtrl.Attribute) CLR(Ref_CSMsgCtrl.Instance) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When Polling is not active, zero out the received data to hide it.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_Poll)FLL(0,Ref_CLMsgDest[0],46)FLL(0,Ref_DTMsgDest[0],17)FLL(0,Ref_CSMsgDest[0],3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONTROLLER CHECK VALUE
============================================================
Take the low-order byte of each of the following to build the
controller CHECK Value (Val_Check):

Change Log Index
Change Log Generation
Software UID
Copy UID]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[BTD(Wrk_CurrIndex,0,Val_Check,0,8)BTD(Wrk_CurrGen,0,Val_Check,8,8)BTD(Wrk_CurrSWUID,0,Val_Check,16,8)BTD(Wrk_CurrCopyUID,0,Val_Check,24,8);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
REPORT CHANGE DETECT STATUS
============================================================
This rung and the four that follow it report specific types of
changes detected.  The Status bits are latched in until
the "Ack All" Command is issued (see above).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[NEQ(Wrk_CurrIndex,Wrk_PrevIndex) ,NEQ(Wrk_CurrGen,Wrk_PrevGen) ]OTL(Wrk_OnlineChange);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Wrk_CurrImgUID,Wrk_PrevImgUID)OTL(Wrk_ChangeDownload);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Wrk_CurrSWUID,Wrk_PrevSWUID)OTL(Wrk_NoChangeDownload);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Wrk_CurrCopyUID,Wrk_PrevCopyUID)OTL(Wrk_EditsDownload);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Wrk_CurrTLUID,Wrk_PrevTLUID)OTL(Wrk_RestoreFromFlash);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copy the internal (protected) latched data out to public Status bits.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_OnlineChange) OTE(Sts_OnlineChange) ,XIC(Wrk_ChangeDownload) OTE(Sts_ChangeDownload) ,XIC(Wrk_NoChangeDownload) OTE(Sts_NoChangeDownload) ,XIC(Wrk_EditsDownload) OTE(Sts_EditsDownload) ,XIC(Wrk_RestoreFromFlash) OTE(Sts_RestoreFromFlash) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
REPORT CONTROLLER STATUS
============================================================
This rung breaks down the bits returned in the the Controller Status:

* Controller Mode (Fault, Run, Prog)
* Fault Status (Major, Minor / Revoverable, Unrecoverable)
* Keyswitch Position (Run, Rem, Prog)

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Ref_CSMsgCtrl.ER)[XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].6) XIO(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].5) XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].4) OTE(Sts_FaultMode) ,XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].6) XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].5) XIO(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].4) OTE(Sts_RunMode) ,XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].6) XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].5) XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].4) OTE(Sts_ProgMode) ,XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].8) OTE(Sts_MinorRecovFlt) ,XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].9) OTE(Sts_MinorUnrecovFlt) ,XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].10) OTE(Sts_MajorRecovFlt) ,XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].11) OTE(Sts_MajorUnrecovFlt) ,XIO(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].13) XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].12) OTE(Sts_KeyswRun) ,XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].13) XIO(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].12) OTE(Sts_KeyswProg) ,XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].13) XIC(Ref_CSMsgDest[3].12) OTE(Sts_KeyswRem) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[* If the instruction is in the midst of polling (messaging) the
necessary data from the controller of interest,
show the Busy status.
*  If the Update timer is timing but the poll is NOT busy,
show the Timing status.
(Sts_MsgErr and Sts_Done are written from latches above.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Poll) OTE(Sts_Busy) ,XIC(Wrk_Done) OTE(Sts_Done) ,XIC(Wrk_MsgErr) OTE(Sts_MsgErr) ,XIC(Wrk_UpdateT.TT) XIO(Wrk_Poll) OTE(Sts_Timing) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear "lurking" commands; reset update timer and poll status]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PRESCAN (POWERUP) HANDLING
============================================================
On Prescan, reset the Update timer and clear the polling status.

NOTE: There is no need to clear the "previous" index and generation data.
Putting the controller in RUN is a change that will be detected (and alarmed)!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[RES(Wrk_UpdateT)OTU(Wrk_Poll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Commands are cleared.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Cmd_AckAll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
